# BB-Checklist

Condensed pre-flight and per-target checklist. Pair with the full methodology in [`README.md`](README.md). Tick items as you go; not every item applies to every program — use judgment.

---

## Pre-Engagement

- [ ] Read program scope **in full** — in-scope assets, out-of-scope assets, testing rules
- [ ] Note prohibited activities (DoS, social eng., physical, automated scanning limits)
- [ ] Note rate-limit / volume rules
- [ ] Note severity matrix and known-issue list
- [ ] Set Burp/Caido scope to match in-scope assets exactly
- [ ] Configure upstream proxy (residential / VPN) if program requires
- [ ] Set unique user-agent if program requires attribution
- [ ] Create two test accounts (for IDOR/BAC testing) where allowed

---

## Recon

### Org / Multi-Domain
- [ ] ASN → IP ranges mapped
- [ ] Acquisitions / subsidiaries identified
- [ ] Reverse-whois pivots run
- [ ] Favicon / trademark hash pivots run
- [ ] GitHub org & employees searched for leaks

### Per Domain
- [ ] Passive subdomain enum (Amass, Subfinder, Assetfinder, crt.sh)
- [ ] Active bruteforce (PureDNS + wordlist)
- [ ] Permutation set (Gotator / alterx)
- [ ] Resolved via dnsx, probed via httpx
- [ ] Subdomain takeover scan (nuclei, subzy)
- [ ] Cloud asset sweep (cloud_enum, S3Scanner)
- [ ] Visual recon (gowitness)
- [ ] Historical URLs collected (gau, waybackurls)

### Per Host
- [ ] Tech fingerprint (httpx, Wappalyzer)
- [ ] Common files checked (`robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `.well-known/`, `.git/`, `.env`)
- [ ] Full crawl + passive URL merge
- [ ] Content discovery (feroxbuster / ffuf)
- [ ] Parameter discovery (Arjun / x8)
- [ ] Nuclei sweep (medium+ severity)
- [ ] All JS files pulled and reviewed

---

## Network

- [ ] Full TCP scan (`nmap -p-`)
- [ ] Service version detection (`-sCV` on open ports)
- [ ] UDP top 200 ports
- [ ] TLS audit (testssl.sh)
- [ ] DMARC / SPF / DKIM check
- [ ] Exposed admin services flagged (Redis, Mongo, Elasticsearch, Docker API, Kubernetes API)

---

## JavaScript

- [ ] All JS files collected (subjs / katana)
- [ ] Endpoints extracted (LinkFinder / xnLinkFinder / JSluice)
- [ ] Secrets scan (trufflehog / SecretFinder / Nosey Parker)
- [ ] Source maps pulled (if present)
- [ ] DOM sinks reviewed manually
- [ ] postMessage handlers reviewed

---

## API

### REST
- [ ] OpenAPI / Swagger / docs endpoint located
- [ ] Verb tampering tested on key endpoints
- [ ] Content-type swap tested
- [ ] Mass assignment payloads tried
- [ ] Rate-limit bypass headers tested
- [ ] Old API versions probed

### GraphQL
- [ ] Introspection enabled? (or use clairvoyance)
- [ ] IDE accessible (`/graphiql`, `/playground`)?
- [ ] Field suggestions on
- [ ] Batching / aliasing tested
- [ ] Sensitive mutations enumerated

---

## Authentication

- [ ] Username enumeration (login / register / reset / timing)
- [ ] Password policy reviewed
- [ ] Brute force / lockout behavior tested
- [ ] 2FA bypass attempts (response tamper, rate limit, reuse)
- [ ] Password reset — token reuse, host header injection, multi-email
- [ ] OAuth flow — `redirect_uri`, `state`, scope
- [ ] SAML — signature wrapping, comment injection (if applicable)
- [ ] JWT — `alg: none`, weak HMAC secret, `kid` injection
- [ ] Magic links — entropy, expiry, reuse

---

## Session

- [ ] Session ID regenerated on login (fixation)
- [ ] CSRF tokens validated server-side and bound to user
- [ ] Cookie flags: `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite`
- [ ] Logout invalidates server-side
- [ ] Token reusable after logout? (must be no)

---

## Authorization (IDOR / BAC)

- [ ] Horizontal swap tested on every resource ID
- [ ] Vertical — low-priv user hitting admin endpoints directly
- [ ] Method-based — endpoint hidden in UI accessible via direct request
- [ ] Parameter pollution (`?user=a&user=b`)
- [ ] Autorize / AuthMatrix run across the app
- [ ] UUID v1 vs v4 checked (predictability)
- [ ] Tenant isolation tested in multi-tenant apps

---

## Input Handling

- [ ] Reflected XSS sweep (Dalfox)
- [ ] Stored XSS — every user-controlled field that renders to others
- [ ] DOM XSS via DOM Invader
- [ ] Blind XSS payloads planted in admin-facing fields
- [ ] SQLi probed (manual + sqlmap where allowed)
- [ ] NoSQLi operators tested on JSON inputs
- [ ] SSRF — all URL-accepting params tested incl. blind/OOB
- [ ] SSTI polyglot probe
- [ ] XXE — every XML / SVG / OOXML upload point
- [ ] LFI / path traversal — all file params
- [ ] Command injection — separators on any system-call-adjacent input
- [ ] Prototype pollution — `__proto__` in JSON bodies and URL params
- [ ] File upload — extension, MIME, magic bytes, zip slip

---

## Business Logic

- [ ] Multi-step flows replayed / reordered / skipped
- [ ] Price / quantity manipulation (negative, decimal, huge, overflow)
- [ ] Coupon / promo stacking, reuse, race-apply
- [ ] Workflow gates bypassable (KYC, age, ToS)
- [ ] Client-side validation only? Tamper to confirm
- [ ] Currency confusion / rounding edge cases

---

## Race Conditions

- [ ] Single-packet attack on coupon/voucher redemption
- [ ] Race on MFA verify / OTP submit
- [ ] Race on follow / vote / like / withdraw / withdraw-to-bank
- [ ] Turbo Intruder race.py prepared

---

## Request Smuggling

- [ ] CL.TE / TE.CL / TE.TE checked (smuggler, Burp HRS extension)
- [ ] HTTP/2 downgrade smuggling checked
- [ ] Impact confirmed before reporting (no probe-only reports)

---

## Cloud

- [ ] S3 buckets enumerated and ACLs checked
- [ ] GCP / Azure equivalents
- [ ] SSRF → metadata service tested
- [ ] Origin IP disclosure (CloudFail) where CDN is between you and origin
- [ ] Public AWS keys / GCP service account JSON in JS or GitHub?

---

## Misc

- [ ] Security header review (informational on most programs)
- [ ] CAPTCHA reuse / removal / OCR
- [ ] Open redirect — kept on hand as chain primitive
- [ ] Cache poisoning (Param Miner)
- [ ] Web cache deception
- [ ] Email header injection on contact forms

---

## Pre-Submit (per report)

- [ ] Reproducible from clean session
- [ ] Steps numbered, no missing context
- [ ] Impact tied to **this program's** assets and data
- [ ] No unrelated findings bundled in
- [ ] Screenshot / short video attached, own creds redacted
- [ ] Severity reasoned, not just claimed
- [ ] Remediation suggestion included, brief
- [ ] No automated-scanner output dumped raw

---

## Post-Submit Hygiene

- [ ] Findings logged privately with timestamps
- [ ] No public disclosure before program permits
- [ ] Follow-up scheduled — don't ghost triage
- [ ] If duped, note the public reference and move on
